  "post": {
    "caption": "Some rings spell words with their gems. Each gem's first letter adds one letter to the word, so six gems can spell REGARD, from a ruby to a diamond, and DEAREST takes seven gems and ends with a topaz or turquoise. The fashion is believed to have started in France, and it was popular from about the 1820s through Victorian times. Givers sent them as tokens of love or friendship, and the stones were often small and set in a row. Some words used the first letters of French gem names, and for V jewelers sometimes used vermeil, an old name for garnet. Empress Josephine owned bracelets that spell her children's names.",
